{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_0125Byqv7yrJuNrwvAuwiLzY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/05-020-ab-testing-for-prompt-variations.md`** covering:\n\n- **Concept:** treating prompt changes as statistically-valid experiments rather than gut-feel comparisons\n- **Mechanism:** 5-step framework — hypothesis + metric selection (primary + guardrails), experiment surface choice (offline golden set → shadow → canary → interleaved), non-determinism controls (T=0 + paired sampling), statistical validity (paired t-test / Mann-Whitney, power analysis, Bonferroni for multi-variant), rollout gate with auto-rollback\n- **Tooling:** promptfoo, LangSmith, RAGAS, Grafana canary dashboards\n- **Concrete example:** support chatbot CoT prompt test — 3.7 vs 3.2 LLM-judge, +4pp deflection, +180ms latency, LLMLingua post-processing to recover latency\n- **3 pitfalls:** eyeballing outputs, ignoring guardrail metrics, 24h canary (novelty spike)\n- **Cross-links** to Q21 (canary/shadow deployment), Q10 (non-deterministic testing), Q16 (formal eval framework)\n\n4 items remain in Next: Q21, Q22, Q23, and validate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":279,"cache_read_input_tokens":71749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":279,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a9c2fa8-81cc-486c-8abc-52c250277ea4","uuid":"b501ff3d-30e8-467e-a18a-0e19381f1dcf"}
